  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Organization for Migration Displacement Tracking Matrix</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective analysis of primary data is key to effective advocacy and a well-informed humanitarian response. IOM&apos;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) is feeding directly into global level analysis, including the Internal Displacement Monitoring Centre&#x2019;s (IDMC) annual Global Report on Internal Displacement, where IOM is the second largest provider of data on conflict situations after OCHA; and regularly informs analysis by other humanitarian and policy actors. This project aims to leverage IOM&#x2019;s DTM global capacity and field implementation in 20 target countries to (1) enhance collection, analysis, management and production of data and information on internal displacement across complex contexts worldwide, which informs humanitarian response plans, as well as other strategic response plans; (2) improve ability for humanitarian partners to more effectively meet the needs of populations affected by humanitarian crises; and, (3) strengthen ability of donors to better prioritize their resources to reach those most in need.</narrative>
  </description>
